<figure class="pixel-figure pixel-wide" data-comparison>
  <div class="pixel-toolbar"><span class="pixel-title">Same tokens, two renderers</span><label for="code-copies">Code copies <output data-copies-value>1</output></label><input id="code-copies" type="range" min="1" max="10" value="1" /></div>
  <div class="pixel-comparison-grid">
    <div><div class="pixel-measure"><span>Token spans</span><strong data-span-count>—</strong><span>elements</span></div><div class="pixel-count-track"><span data-span-bar></span></div><pre class="pixel-comparison-code"><code data-span-code></code></pre></div>
    <div><div class="pixel-measure"><span>Color image</span><strong data-pixel-count>—</strong><span>elements</span></div><div class="pixel-count-track"><span data-pixel-bar></span></div><pre class="pixel-comparison-code"><code class="pixel-text" data-comparison-code>JavaScript generates both renderings from the same tokens.</code></pre></div>
  </div>
  <figcaption data-comparison-caption>Counts include each pre and code, and token spans where present. Controls and labels are excluded. This measures DOM size, not speed.</figcaption>
